1,Afroasiatic languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afroasiatic_languages,"Afroasiatic languages ... The Afroasiatic languages (also known as the Afro-Asiatic, Afrasian, Hamito-Semitic, or Semito-Hamitic languages) are a language family (or phylum) of about 400 languages spoken predominantly in West Asia, North Africa, the Horn of Africa, and parts of the Sahara and Sahel. [4]",Taznatit,Afro-Asiatic
